<title>UK: Hungary's electricity companies to float - Csiha.</title>
<headline>Hungary's electricity companies to float - Csiha.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's handful of privatised electricity companies will be floated on the Budapest stock exchange this year, Privatisation Minister Judit Csiha told Reuters in an interview on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;They will be floated on the Budapest stock exchange during the course of this year for sure,&quot; Csiha said, on the last day of a three-day visit to London.</p>
<p>&quot;Those companies that meet the appropriate requirements will be floated,&quot; she said, adding that Budapest Electricity Works was the most ready to be floated.  </p>
<p>The market has been waiting for an announcement on this decision, sources said.</p>
<p>Hungary sold minority stakes in six regional electricity distributors to strategic investors in 1995.  </p>
<p>-- Hayley Pienaar, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7718</p>
